WEBVTT

00:00:02.899 --> 00:00:09.550
<v Priya Raman>Morning, everyone. Tuesday the sixteenth of June. Can you all hear me, or am I talking to myself again?</v>

00:00:11.259 --> 00:00:18.260
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, got you. Hard to hear anything over the heating in the portakabin, mind. It's June and I'm being slow-roasted.</v>

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:21.940
<v Marcus Hale>Luxury. Usually it's like sitting in a fridge.</v>

00:00:23.609 --> 00:00:27.109
<v Olumide Adeyemi>There is apparently no setting between fridge and blast furnace.</v>

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:35.979
<v Hannah Price>Speaking of ovens, the charity bake sale on Friday. Judging by last time, I'm buying something rather than baking.</v>

00:00:37.689 --> 00:00:39.090
<v David Whitfield>Probably kinder to everyone.</v>

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:41.380
<v Hannah Price>Cheers. Lovely supportive team, this.</v>

00:00:41.979 --> 00:00:46.530
<v Priya Raman>Right, before this becomes a disciplinary. Finished stuff first, then what's actually ours.</v>

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:53.450
<v Hannah Price>I tested the Line 2 Safety Guard Interlock yesterday and it's all fine now. That's done.</v>

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:58.409
<v Priya Raman>And that's the completed one, not another test going on today's list?</v>

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:02.109
<v Hannah Price>Exactly. Closed out yesterday. Just feeding back.</v>

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:12.579
<v Marcus Hale>Same sort of thing from me: signed off the inspection on the Site Water System on Tuesday. Already signed off, nothing new there.</v>

00:01:13.989 --> 00:01:17.140
<v Priya Raman>Good, both of those stay in the done pile.</v>

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:25.180
<v Aisha Begum>Um, observations only from me. Heard a slight rattle from the turbine one, nothing to action yet.</v>

00:01:25.769 --> 00:01:29.620
<v Marcus Hale>Right, an observation, not you asking for someone to strip it.</v>

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:37.700
<v Aisha Begum>Definitely not. Also saw the pressure on the Gas Turbine 2 dip for a few minutes, it came back on its own.</v>

00:01:38.299 --> 00:01:41.450
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, talking over you—came back without anyone doing anything?</v>

00:01:42.829 --> 00:01:47.730
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, on its own. Just reporting what I saw, no new job off that.</v>

00:01:50.189 --> 00:01:55.090
<v Aisha Begum>And the shutdown on the booster pump is cancelled now, production need it running.</v>

00:01:56.879 --> 00:01:59.680
<v Fiona Doyle>Right, cancelled rather than pushed back a bit?</v>

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:04.269
<v Priya Raman>Cancelled. We're not carrying that shutdown as work to do today.</v>

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:14.439
<v Fiona Doyle>On blockers, the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the Line 3 Chiller. That's still stuck, not something I can put into the running plan.</v>

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:20.370
<v Priya Raman>Understood. Blocked status, not another action out of this meeting.</v>

00:02:21.289 --> 00:02:26.539
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the turbine one either. Same story.</v>

00:02:27.289 --> 00:02:29.389
<v David Whitfield>Lots of certainty from suppliers, then.</v>

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:34.379
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Consistently uncertain. Anyway, still blocked; no new work to report on that.</v>

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:40.610
<v Priya Raman>Okay. Actual jobs now. There's one that needs to cut straight through the usual queue.</v>

00:02:41.069 --> 00:02:48.419
<v Priya Raman>Han, can you go to the substation to pick up the replacement parts for the BFP? Drop everything for that one.</v>

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:56.919
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, I'll go to the substation and pick up the replacement parts for the BFP. Understood on dropping everything.</v>

00:02:57.969 --> 00:03:02.520
<v Priya Raman>Thanks. That's the priority for you, not something to fit round the edges.</v>

00:03:04.169 --> 00:03:05.370
<v Hannah Price>Yep, clear.</v>

00:03:06.629 --> 00:03:12.229
<v Priya Raman>I'll do the pre-use checks on the trucks this morning. That one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:03:13.849 --> 00:03:20.150
<v David Whitfield>Got it, Priya Raman on the pre-use checks on the trucks. Not waiting till later in the morning.</v>

00:03:20.599 --> 00:03:21.800
<v Priya Raman>Exactly, straight away.</v>

00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:29.520
<v Aisha Begum>We also need someone to check the guarding on the palletiser. That one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:37.180
<v Priya Raman>Right. Who can actually take the guarding check? I don't want a general nod being mistaken for an owner.</v>

00:03:37.509 --> 00:03:39.610
<v David Whitfield>I can't take that one. Sorry.</v>

00:03:41.229 --> 00:03:45.780
<v Hannah Price>Nor me, with the BFP parts taking priority. Don't put me against it.</v>

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:50.879
<v Priya Raman>Okay, nobody's taken the palletiser guarding check. It stays explicitly unowned.</v>

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:57.610
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah. Unowned doesn't make it less urgent, though. Still safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:03:59.159 --> 00:04:03.710
<v Priya Raman>Agreed. Separately, I'll schedule downtime for the dryer with production tomorrow at 9:30.</v>

00:04:06.129 --> 00:04:11.030
<v Fiona Doyle>Tomorrow at 9:30 for that, yeah? Just making sure I heard the half past.</v>

00:04:12.569 --> 00:04:16.069
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, tomorrow at 9:30. I'll handle scheduling it with production.</v>

00:04:18.079 --> 00:04:24.379
<v David Whitfield>I'll run a function test on the PRV on the boiler this afternoon. No rush on that one.</v>

00:04:24.939 --> 00:04:31.240
<v Marcus Hale>Right, David Whitfield for the PRV on the boiler, this afternoon, no rush. Separate from the urgent bits.</v>

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:35.839
<v David Whitfield>That's it. I'll take that test.</v>

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:43.170
<v Priya Raman>Fi, can you do a site visit at Northfield with the contractor by the end of the week? No rush.</v>

00:04:45.329 --> 00:04:51.980
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, I'll do the site visit at Northfield with the contractor. By the end of the week is fine.</v>

00:04:54.189 --> 00:04:58.040
<v Priya Raman>Lovely. No rush, as I say, just within that end-of-week limit.</v>

00:04:58.769 --> 00:05:02.970
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep, understood. It doesn't need squeezing in ahead of the urgent stuff.</v>

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:11.279
<v Priya Raman>Han, could you organise the toolbox talk for the team by Thursday, if you've got a spare minute?</v>

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:19.689
<v Hannah Price>Sorry, no, I can't take that as well. Especially with dropping everything for the parts. That needs to go to someone else.</v>

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:30.149
<v Priya Raman>Fair enough. Fiona, can I hand that to you instead—organise the toolbox talk for the team by Thursday, if you've got a spare minute?</v>

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:37.850
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, I'll take it instead. I'll organise the toolbox talk for the team by Thursday.</v>

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:42.949
<v Hannah Price>Thanks. Better than me saying yes and it disappearing under everything else.</v>

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:49.470
<v Fiona Doyle>And we're saying organised by Thursday, not saying the talk itself has to happen on Thursday?</v>

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:54.750
<v Priya Raman>Correct, organised by Thursday. That's all we're agreeing there.</v>

00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:59.060
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Look at that, a meeting where saying no actually worked.</v>

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:05.860
<v Aisha Begum>Don't sound so surprised. You nearly came off mute twice for that one.</v>

00:06:06.649 --> 00:06:12.949
<v Priya Raman>Quick read-back, then. Han's got the replacement parts for the BFP from the substation, dropping everything for it.</v>

00:06:13.589 --> 00:06:14.790
<v Hannah Price>Yep, mine.</v>

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:21.490
<v David Whitfield>And mine's the function test on the PRV on the boiler this afternoon. No rush.</v>

00:06:22.779 --> 00:06:32.230
<v Fiona Doyle>I've got Northfield with the contractor by the end of the week, no rush, and organising the toolbox talk by Thursday, if I've got a spare minute.</v>

00:06:32.949 --> 00:06:41.699
<v Priya Raman>I've got the pre-use checks on the trucks this morning, safety critical, straight away; and scheduling downtime for the dryer with production tomorrow at 9:30.</v>

00:06:43.490 --> 00:06:50.139
<v Aisha Begum>And just so it doesn't vanish in the summary, the palletiser guarding still needs checking. Nobody has accepted that.</v>

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:57.129
<v Priya Raman>Correct. No owner agreed for that one, and the safety-critical, straight-away urgency stands. I'm not marking it as covered.</v>

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:02.759
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Right, all clear from me. Assuming I haven't melted into this chair.</v>

00:07:04.399 --> 00:07:06.500
<v Priya Raman>All right, thanks everyone. That's us.</v>
